// SOURCE: examples/gpu/life/main.vl
// REQUIRES: metal
// LINK: std::gpu and std::window name the frameworks they link
// (0.25.4) The window's own event loop with no display, driven by a
// script (std::window, VOLE_WINDOW_SCRIPT): space pauses, c clears, g
// hides the grid lines, a left drag paints a band, n steps one generation
// (the band becomes its outline), and the next frame presented is the shot.
// ARGS: --grid 64
// ENV: VOLE_WINDOW_SCRIPT=size 320x200; frames 2; key space; key c; key g; press left 100 100; move 220 100; release left 220 100; key n; shot life-script.ppm; frames 1
// EXPECT-PPM: life-script.ppm tests/golden/gpu-life-script.ppm region 84,80,156,40 tolerance 8 allow 1%
